  "miqat": "Miqat",
  "mekatInstruction1Title": "Bathing and Perfuming",
  "mekatInstruction1Desc": "It is recommended for a Muslim to bathe and apply perfume before Ihram.\n\n• Bathing is a confirmed Sunnah before Ihram\n• A man applies perfume to his body (not to the Ihram clothes)\n• A woman avoids perfume if she will intermingle with men\n\nThe purpose of this is:\n• Cleanliness\n• Preparing to enter the ritual",
  "mekatInstruction2Title": "Wearing Ihram Clothes",
  "mekatInstruction2Desc": "How to wear Ihram clothes:\n\nFor men:\n• Wear an Izar and a Rida (two unsewn pieces of cloth)\n• Do not cover the head\n• Wear sandals (preferably open)\n\nFor women:\n• Wear normal modest clothing (without adornment)\n• No specific color is required\n• Do not wear the Niqab or gloves\n\nNotes:\n• Clothes must be clean\n• Use of perfume is prohibited after Ihram",
  "mekatInstruction3Title": "Intention",
  "mekatInstruction3Desc": "Intention is the entering into the ritual.\n\n• Its place is the heart (verbalization is not required)\n• It is recommended to say:\n\"Labbayk Allahumma Umrah\"\n\nNotes:\n• Intention should be made upon reaching the Miqat\n• Ihram is not valid without intention",
  "mekatInstruction4Title": "Miqat",
  "mekatInstruction4Desc": "The Miqat is the place from which Ihram must be assumed.\n\n• It is not permissible to pass it without Ihram for those intending Umrah\n\nFamous Miqats:\n• Dhu'l-Hulayfah (People of Madinah)\n• Al-Juhfah (People of Sham)\n• Qarn al-Manazil (People of Najd)\n• Yalamlam (People of Yemen)\n• Dhat Irq (People of Iraq)\n\nNotes:\n• Those within the Miqat boundaries assume Ihram from their place\n• Those in an airplane assume Ihram when parallel to the Miqat",
  "mekatInstruction5Title": "Talbiyah",
  "mekatInstruction5Desc": "The pilgrim begins the Talbiyah immediately after assuming Ihram.\n\nText of the Talbiyah:\n\"Labbayk Allahumma Umrah, Labbayka la sharika laka Labbayk, Innal-hamda wan-ni'mata laka wal-mulk, la sharika lak\"\n\nWhen to say it:\n• Immediately after the intention\n• Repeated during the way to Makkah\n\nNotes:\n• A man raises his voice with it\n• A woman says it in a low voice\n• It continues until the start of Tawaf",
  "tawaf": "Tawaf",
  "tawafInstruction1Title": "Entering Al-Masjid Al-Haram",
  "tawafInstruction1Desc": "When entering Al-Masjid Al-Haram:\n\n• Enter with the right foot\n• Say: \"Bismillah, Allahumma salli 'ala Muhammad\"\n• And say: \"Allahumma-ftah li abwaba rahmatik\"\n\nNotes:\n• Enter with tranquility and calmness\n• Do not crowd people\n• Recall the greatness of the place",
  "tawafInstruction2Title": "At the Black Stone",
  "tawafInstruction2Desc": "Upon reaching the Black Stone:\n\n• If possible: Touch it with your right hand and kiss it\n• If you cannot: Touch it with your hand and kiss your hand\n• If you cannot: Point to it with your hand and say \"Allahu Akbar\"\n\nNotes:\n• Do not harm others by crowding\n• Pointing is sufficient during crowding",
  "tawafInstruction3Title": "Tawaf around the Kaaba",
  "tawafInstruction3Desc": "How to perform Tawaf:\n\n• Keep the Kaaba to your left\n• Start from the Black Stone\n• Perform 7 complete rounds\n\nNotes:\n• Each round starts and ends at the Black Stone\n• It is recommended to hasten slightly (Raml) for men in the first 3 rounds\n• Normal walking in the remaining rounds",
  "tawafInstruction4Title": "Remembrance and Supplication during Tawaf",
  "tawafInstruction4Desc": "During Tawaf:\n\n• Increase remembrance and supplication\n• Read what is easy of the Quran\n\nIt is recommended between the Yemeni Corner and the Black Stone:\n\"Rabbana atina fid-dunya hasanatan wa fil-akhirati hasanatan wa qina 'adhaban-nar\"\n\nNotes:\n• There is no specific supplication for each round\n• Supplicate for whatever you wish",
  "tawafInstruction5Title": "Praying two Raka'ahs after Tawaf",
  "tawafInstruction5Desc": "After finishing Tawaf:\n\n• Pray two Raka'ahs behind Maqam Ibrahim if possible\n• If not possible, pray anywhere in the Masjid\n\nIn the two Raka'ahs:\n• Read Al-Fatihah\n• Preferably read:\n  - Al-Kafirun in the first\n  - Al-Ikhlas in the second\n\nNotes:\n• Do not crowd people at the Maqam",
  "makamInstruction1Title": "Heading to Maqam Ibrahim",
  "makamInstruction1Desc": "After finishing Tawaf:\n\n• Head to Maqam Ibrahim if possible\n• Place the Maqam between yourself and the Kaaba\n\nAllah Almighty said:\n\"And take, [O believers], from the standing place of Abraham a place of prayer\"\n\nNotes:\n• It is not necessary to stand directly next to the Maqam\n• You can pray anywhere inside the Mosque",
  "makamInstruction2Title": "Praying two Rak'ahs",
  "makamInstruction2Desc": "Pray two Rak'ahs after Tawaf:\n\n• The first Rak'ah:\n  - Al-Fatiha\n  - Surah Al-Kafirun (recommended)\n\n• The second Rak'ah:\n  - Al-Fatiha\n  - Surah Al-Ikhlas (recommended)\n\nNotes:\n• Prayer is a confirmed Sunnah after Tawaf\n• Do not crowd people for the sake of praying at the Maqam",
  "makamInstruction3Title": "Prayer Place",
  "makamInstruction3Desc": "Prayer Place:\n\n• Best: Behind Maqam Ibrahim\n• If not possible due to crowding:\n  - Pray anywhere inside the Grand Mosque\n\nNotes:\n• Avoid extreme crowding\n• Reverence is better than proximity",
  "makamInstruction4Title": "After Prayer",
  "makamInstruction4Desc": "After finishing the two Rak'ahs:\n\n• Drink from Zamzam water if possible\n• Supplicate to Allah as you wish\n• Prepare to go for Sa'i between Safa and Marwa\n\nNotes:\n• Zamzam water is Sunnah, not obligatory\n• It is recommended to supplicate a lot",
  "pleaseCompleteInstructions": "Please complete all instructions to proceed",
  "pleaseReadInstructionsCarefully": "Please read the instructions carefully to perform Tawaf correctly",
  "pleaseVerifyMapFirst": "Please complete map verification first",
  "prayerBehindMakam": "Prayer behind the Station of Ibrahim",
  "makamIbrahim": "Maqam Ibrahim",
  "sai": "Sa'i between Safa and Marwa",
  "safaMarwaInstruction1Title": "Heading to Safa",
  "safaMarwaInstruction1Desc": "After finishing Tawaf and praying two Raka'ahs:\n\n• Head to Safa Hill to start Sa'i\n• When approaching, read:\n\"Innas-Safa wal-Marwata min sha'a'irillah\"\n\nNotes:\n• This verse is said once at the beginning of Sa'i",
  "safaMarwaInstruction2Title": "Standing on Safa",
  "safaMarwaInstruction2Desc": "Upon ascending Safa Hill:\n\n• Face the Kaaba if possible\n• Raise your hands and supplicate to Allah\n\nIt is recommended to say:\n\"Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar\nLa ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah...\"\n\nNotes:\n• Repeat the remembrance and supplication 3 times\n• Supplicate for whatever good you wish of this world and the hereafter",
  "safaMarwaInstruction3Title": "Sa'i between Safa and Marwa",
  "safaMarwaInstruction3Desc": "Start Sa'i from Safa to Marwa:\n\n• Set your direction toward Marwa\n• At the two green markers:\n  - Men hasten (light jogging)\n  - Women walk normally\n\nNotes:\n• The rest of the distance is normal walking\n• Increase remembrance and supplication",
  "safaMarwaInstruction4Title": "Number of Rounds",
  "safaMarwaInstruction4Desc": "Number of Sa'i rounds:\n\n• 7 complete rounds\n\nThe method:\n• From Safa to Marwa = round 1\n• From Marwa to Safa = round 2\n• And so on until you finish at Marwa\n\nNotes:\n• Start from Safa\n• End at Marwa",
  "safaMarwaInstruction5Title": "Supplication during Sa'i",
  "safaMarwaInstruction5Desc": "During Sa'i:\n\n• Increase supplication and remembrance\n• Read what is easy of the Quran\n\nNotes:\n• There is no specific supplication for each round\n• Supplicate for whatever you love",
  "safaMarwaInstruction6Title": "After finishing Sa'i",
  "safaMarwaInstruction6Desc": "After completing 7 rounds:\n\n• You have finished Sa'i\n• Prepare for shaving or cutting hair\n\nNotes:\n• Sa'i is a pillar of Umrah\n• Umrah is not valid without it",
